  "question": {
    "text": "The correct nucleophilicity order is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "mdGIR",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}^{-}<\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}<\\mathrm{HO}^{-}<\\mathrm{F}^{-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AfbO0",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}^{-} \\simeq \\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}>\\mathrm{HO}^{-} \\simeq \\mathrm{F}^{-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LxQ5f",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}^{-}>\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}>\\mathrm{HO}^{-}>\\mathrm{F}^{-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "FEkJU",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}>\\mathrm{F}^{-}>\\mathrm{HO}^{-}>\\mathrm{CH}_{3}^{-}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Nucleophilicity increases with the decrease in electronegativity of the central atom. Since electronegativity follows the order:\n$\\mathrm{F}>\\mathrm{O}>\\mathrm{N}>\\mathrm{C} ;$ nucleophilicity of the\nconcerned group will follow the reverse order i.e.,\n$\\mathrm{CH}_{3}^{-}>\\mathrm{NH}_{2}^{-}>\\mathrm{OH}^{-}>\\mathrm{F}^{-}$",
    "image": null
  },
